.TH WHICH 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
which \- locate a command in PATH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B which
.I command
.RI [ command ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B which
searches each directory listed in the
.B PATH
environment variable, in order, for each
.I command
name given and prints the full path of the first match to standard output.
.PP
If a command is not found in any
.B PATH
directory, its name is reported to standard error.
After processing all arguments,
.B which
exits 1 if any command was not found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "which ls"
Print the full path of
.BR ls .
.TP
.B "which ls grep cat"
Print the paths of all three commands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All commands were found.
.TP
.B 1
No arguments were given, or one or more commands could not be found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR which (1),
.BR type (1),
.BR hako (1)
